The shield doesn't impede spellcasting much if at all; the iron helm does
(not much either, but it may be wise to take it off to cast things like
identify).

> One good weapon type for wizards is dagger. They can get to expert in
> it, and will receive Magicbane as a first gift, which is a very useful
> weapon. Wield an elven dagger 

And #name it Sting even if you're Neutral; the orc warning and web-cutting
is useful and it doesn't cost anything. It doesn't hurt your chance of
Magicbane from sacrifice either. 

If you have a silver dagger (they're quite rare) consider wielding that
instead.

> and collect normal ones for throwing. 
> Build up a good throwing stack and make ranged combat with daggers and
> spells your priority. Advance dagger skill instead of quarterstaff.

Very good advice. And if your god happens to give you an artifact
longsword after the Magicbane, practice just enough with it to get it up
to Basic (doesn't get any higher anyway).

